      "extract": "Concentration inequalities bound tail probabilities of general functions of random variables. Several methods have been known to prove such inequalities, including martingale methods, information theoretic methods, Talagrand's induction method as well as a variety of problem-specific methods. Ledoux (see \\cite{Led} for a survey) developed a powerful framework known as the \"entropy method\" for proving concentration",
